# Advisor Pipeline Architecture (FR-7.1)

## The 3 Layers — Never Bypass
```
Layer 1: Deterministic Calculations (engines/services)  → numeric facts
Layer 2: Rule Engine (advisor/rules/*)                  → flags + recommendations
Layer 3: AI Explanation (advisor/ai/AiExplainerService)  → plain-English summary
```

## Priority Order (fixed, from spec)
1. Goal Adequacy  2. Emergency Fund  3. Debt Management  4. Insurance Gaps
5. Asset Allocation  6. Contribution Adequacy  7. Investment Selection  8. Tax Optimization

## Rules
- New rules MUST implement the `Rule` interface with a unique priority number
- Rules MUST be stateless — all data comes from `HouseholdFinancialContext`
- Context is built ONCE per advisor run — rules never query the DB directly
- AI layer (Layer 3) SHALL NOT invent calculations or contradict Layer 1 (NFR-5.2)
- If all rules pass → advisor says "do nothing" (empty results list)
- Recommendations are persisted with specVersion for auditability (NFR-7.3)
